  "market_context": "After a strong impulse move that broke prior structure, price entered a large daily consolidation zone. Two Fibonacci retracement entries (long and short) both failed as price broke through the full standard deviation level on both sides.",
  "key_observation": "Price broke the entire standard deviation (Fib extension) twice in succession after two failed Fib retracement trades, signaling a consolidation phase where Fib-based entries are unreliable.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the impulse move that broke previous structure (top to bottom of strongest non-stop momentum candles) to draw Fibonacci retracement.",
    "Step 2: Enter long at the Fibonacci gold zone (0.5–0.618) expecting continuation to previous high, but trade hit stop loss due to news event.",
    "Step 3: After news, reapply same setup: impulse move broken structure → Fib gold zone entry → target previous high.",
    "Step 4: Observe price again breaks full standard deviation downward, then reverses and breaks full standard deviation upward — two consecutive losses.",
    "Step 5: Conclude the market is in consolidation; advise stopping trading, removing indicators, and drawing only a rectangle until price exits the zone."
  ],
  "outcome": "Two consecutive losing trades; analyst advised to stop trading and wait for breakout from consolidation rectangle.",
  "lessons": "When two Fib retracement trades fail back-to-back with price breaking full standard deviation both ways, it signals consolidation—avoid trading until price exits the range.",
